    "created_at": "2026-03-16T16:45:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-16T16:45:33Z",
    "body": "> /cc @mfreed7\r\n\r\nThis looks great to me! I could finally address [this 4 year old Chromium TODO](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_construction_site.cc;l=954;drc=a4e4468cbf6e50c3bf24900f7d34762a44222a72).\r\n\r\n> Right. I think that it would be possible to ship the two independently, right? It's possible today to create a manual assignment shadowroot and never assign nodes.\r\n\r\n+1 - I think this PR provides perfect parity to the imperative `attachShadow()` call, which just sets the `slotAssignment` mode but doesn't actually assign nodes. That might be enough, in that it keeps slots from being automatically assigned to slots before the imperative code boots up and assigns them.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4069088675/reactions",
